================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

The compiled frontend includes @decky/api from the SteamDeckHomebrew project,
licensed under LGPL-2.1. Its exact version, upstream metadata, licence and
unmodified TypeScript/JavaScript source are in third_party/decky-api/.
https://github.com/SteamDeckHomebrew/loader-api

React and @decky/ui are supplied by the Decky host and are not bundled here.

The plugin shells out to `xprop` (xorg-xprop) to read and write the gamescope
atoms. It is already part of SteamOS and is not redistributed here.

`lego_updater.py` originated in the author's other DeckyLoader plugins.
This checkout contains further audit fixes; other repositories are maintained
separately. It is not third-party code.

================================================================================
Prior art
================================================================================

vibrantDeck by Scrumplex (https://github.com/libvibrant/vibrantDeck, LGPL-3.0)
solves the SDR half by writing the same gamescope atom. No code from it is used
here - the atom is a public gamescope interface and this plugin's own
implementation, its HDR half, and its colour maths were written from scratch -
but it deserves the credit for getting there first.

Reading it is also where the idea of detecting resume-from-suspend by comparing
CLOCK_MONOTONIC against CLOCK_BOOTTIME came from, and the observation that
gamescope can clobber these atoms while it re-initialises, so the values have to
go back more than once. The implementation here is independent, but the insight
is theirs and it is worth saying so.
